{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">2023 AMC 10A #9</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2023 AMC 12A #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Ani_lytical_(Comprehensive_🧠)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Ani_lytical (Comprehensive 🧠)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A digital display shows the current date as an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit integer consisting of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit year, followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit month, followed by a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit date within the month. For example, Arbor Day this year is displayed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/f/5cf591fd677741942703c759048baac2f7706037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20230428.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> For how many dates in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> does each digit appear an even number of times in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digital display for that date?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc29d093b21da1a74ea167827248d2b33d982ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~5\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~6\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~7\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~8\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Casework)\">Solution 1 (Casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Do careful casework by each month. Make sure to start with 2023. In the month and the date, we need a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and two digits repeated (which has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> after consideration). After the casework, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21dc45146811933701ee57bf77edf69ea093f299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" />. \nFor curious readers, the numbers (in chronological order) are:\n</p>\n<pre>20230113\n20230131\n20230223\n20230311\n20230322\n20231013\n20231031\n20231103\n20231130\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There is one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so we need one more (three more means that either the month or units digit of the day is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). For the same reason, we need one more <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. By inspection, we can see that the other two digits must be a repeated digit that is not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the units digit of the month, then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> must be the units digit of the month, since there is no month ending with 3 that is more than March. In this case, the last two digits must match (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/b/ecb0c773e05751f2a531d7186f53f70def774f82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11, 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />). This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643ba870c273a8996a60c6a9307c0182aa808be4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-03-11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53153a6a23693bc7bc3a7a38e6e4e6621557db0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-03-22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, so 2 successes.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the tens digit of the day, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> can be in any of the remaining three places. If it is in the ones digit of the the day, then the month must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca0cb888d092a670c0aa374ab233d697155dbc8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-11-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />. If it is in the ones digit of the month, then the month must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, in which case the day must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0511dd52aa0af9ecb0ab000d73a93bc46a4ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-10-31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is in the tens digit of the month, then the month must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/1/ce1ef24f6cf1d8a2ebbbaba89ee70b68c9947414.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$01$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47eb681d2a490b74330536ddcc1d7ccd2ba6b22d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-01-31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />. Together, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/0/ca0cb888d092a670c0aa374ab233d697155dbc8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-11-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0511dd52aa0af9ecb0ab000d73a93bc46a4ffa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-10-31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47eb681d2a490b74330536ddcc1d7ccd2ba6b22d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023-01-31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> make 3 successes. \n</p><p><br />\nIf <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the units digit of the day, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> could go in any of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> remaining slots again. If it's the tens digit of the day, then the other digits must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the units digit of the month, then the other two slots must both be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the tens digit of the month, then the other two slots can be either both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In total, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> successes here. \n</p><p>Summing through all cases, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/c/1cc9447dd9ac16ba5755791a41d1d913ad17452c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 + 4 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"151\" height=\"30\" /> dates. \n</p><p>-Benedict T (countmath1)\n</p><p>-Edits by Cat_Of_Logic\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d061b3e105233ef06361216f1117fe4f21e6cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023----$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"111\" height=\"15\" /> we need an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. So we have at least one of those extras in the days, except we can have the month <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/0/240abf43147c18ed4b6f46db32687a996233306d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$03$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. We now have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possible months <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/2871d1a0f7961e6ce6196611f7931fe611cf2a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$01,02,03,10,11,12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />. For month <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we have two cases, we now have to add in another 1, and the possible days are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a902f1ee572b1b51db56647b287ed7669db0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13,31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" />. For month <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we need an extra <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so we can have the day <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> note that we can't use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because it is to large. Now for month <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we can have any number and multiply it by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> so we have the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a32c46b8500f96ff9f4036da8d282c53fd6af05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11,22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />. For October we need a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a902f1ee572b1b51db56647b287ed7669db0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13,31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> as our choices. For November we have two choices which are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/8/5c8456b2d690ddad96120b35a0913ce32398a72d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$03,30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />.Now for December we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options. Summing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/692ab35b2a581684ccd467d2087c9f974dd4fc4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+1+2+2+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/d/21dc45146811933701ee57bf77edf69ea093f299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}~9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"55\" height=\"30\" /> solutions.\n</p><p>~kyogrexu\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Little Fermat\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=RjE2si8uG_p5xO_2&amp;t=1670\">https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=RjE2si8uG_p5xO_2&amp;t=1670</a>\n~little-fermat\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=iDDNwV-Ut5UZSoQu&amp;t=2010\">https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=iDDNwV-Ut5UZSoQu&amp;t=2010</a>\n</p>\n<pre>~Math-X\n</pre>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28easy_to_digest.29_by_Power_Solve\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(easy_to_digest)_by_Power_Solve\">Video Solution (easy to digest) by Power Solve</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=